I completed all steps, 1 through 6, of the program. To verify:

Build:
You can build either by running the bash script `compileOS.sh` or via make.
Load and boot the resultant file `diskc.img` in the emulator as usual.

Verify:
Once the emulated machine boots you should see the shell prompt "AHOY>"
Enter the provided commands to test the following functionality:
    type messag : This shows that the "type" command is correctly implemented
    type : This prints an error message that the user needs to specify a file
    type asdf : This prints an error message that the file was not found
    exec tstpr2 : This shows that the shell will run again once tstpr2 terminates
    exec : This prints an error message that the user needs to specify a file
    exec asdf : This prints an error message that the file was not found
    type tstpr2 : This prints garbage
    exec messag : This runs garbage!

